 193: ## D. SEAT FINDINGS
 194: 
 195: ### D1. *** codex CANNOT DESIGN WITNESSES FOR THIS PROJECT -- a routing fact, not a failure ***
 196: 
 197: Four briefs on the SAME defect: three answered in full, the witness-design brief refused.
 198: 
 199:     brief                    .err bytes   file reads   outcome
 200:     ARM decode                   70,308   many         ANSWERED
 201:     alphatbinegsel VERIFY        20,210   many         ANSWERED
 202:     alphatbinegsel Q3           167,085   many         ANSWERED
 203:     alphatbinegsel WITNESS        6,291   *** ZERO *** REFUSED (0-byte txt)
 204: 
 205: **Zero file-read lines = it refused before opening anything.**  The prompt's TEXT tripped it.  The
 206: brief used no `kill`/`host dies`/`exploit` vocabulary: **neutral language was NOT sufficient.**  The
 207: distinction is ANALYSING existing code versus CONSTRUCTING a guest sequence that reaches the defect
 208: -- and witness design is inherently the second.
 209: 
 210: **Rerouted to grok BYTE-FOR-BYTE**, which delivered a full design.  That is what makes this a
 211: capability finding rather than a prompt-quality one.
 212: 
 213: **A THREE-STATE DISCRIMINATOR, one `grep -c`:**
 214: 
 215:     refusal line + ZERO reads              PROMPT-LEVEL.  Reroute; a retry will not help.
 216:     refusal line + MANY reads              LATE (archive/subject).  Scoping may help.
 217:     NO refusal line, 0-byte txt, alive     MID-RUN.  Not a refusal.
 218:     NO txt and NO err at all               THE RUN NEVER STARTED -- a launcher fault, not a refusal.
 219: 
 220: *** CORRECTED after I wrote it: an earlier form keyed the first state on "small .err + zero reads",
 221: and that MATCHED A HEALTHY SEAT twenty minutes later -- the pass-2 brief inlines the whole diff, so
 222: codex legitimately read nothing while streaming 39 KB of reasoning.  THE REFUSAL LINE IS THE TEST;
 223: the read count only says WHERE it refused. ***
 224: 
 225: The third state was measured separately tonight: a relative artifacts path in a background shell,
 226: where **the harness reported "completed (exit code 0)"** from the wrapper while the command exited 1
 227: and codex was never invoked.  Only an explicit `echo "EXIT=$?"` caught it.
 228: 
 229: ### D3. *** A FOURTH codex TRIGGER: THE ASK-AGAIN QUESTION ITSELF -- and it is a MANDATED step ***
 230: 
 231: codex ANSWERED the `#513` pass-2 diff review and REFUSED the pass-3 one.  Same round, same file,
 232: same neutral vocabulary, one hour apart.  **The refusal is LATE** (133 KB `.err`, 30,706 tokens,
 233: many file reads), so it is the archive/subject shape, not the chain shape.
 234: 
 235: The difference is pass 3's Q3: *"name the smallest edit that keeps a guard and makes these two rows
 236: GREEN while the latch behaviour is WRONG."*  **That is evasion construction, not source review.**
 237: 
 238: > **The vacuity floor MANDATES exactly that question of every clean kill table, and measured yield
 239: > says it is where the real escapes come from.  So codex is unavailable for the highest-yield
 240: > adversarial query in the round lifecycle, on top of being unavailable for witness design.**
 241: 
 242: **Across nine firings the pattern is consistent: codex reviews CODE THAT EXISTS; it will not
 243: construct an edit or a sequence that defeats something.**  Mitigation is proven -- pass 3's five
 244: other seats all answered it, and grok additionally prescribed the one-row class closure that I
 245: implemented.  **Route the ask-again to grok and the Ollama transports.**
 246: 
 247: ### D2. The scoping remedy has a measured NEGATIVE CONTROL
 248: 
 249: `codexsubjectrefusal`'s recorded remedy is neutral language AND reading scoped to `src/` +
 250: `regress/*.py`.  Applied deliberately and singly to the `sgirekills` re-pin brief: **refused again.**
 251: **Scoping reading to `src/` cannot help when `src/` IS the flagged content** -- a hardening fork's
 252: product source reads to the filter like the archive does.
 253: 
 254: **And the remedy is not free:** on the Alpha VERIFY brief my scoping EXCLUDED the invalidation
 255: callback, so the seat could not settle Q3 and said so.  **Narrowing scope to avoid the filter can
 256: starve the question.**
