   1: # #513 sgirekills -- kill table 1   (scratch clone /tmp/gx513, frozen instrument)
   2: # baseline BASE 44/44   (from BASE.raw, re-derived)
   3: #
   4: # *** THIS LINE READ "42/44" WHEN THE TABLE WAS WRITTEN, WHICH IS M12_linswap's SCORE, NOT THE
   5: # BASELINE'S.  My summary block reused the loop variables `n, d' after the mutant loop had
   6: # reassigned them, so the header printed the LAST mutant's numbers under the baseline's
   7: # label.  Corrected 2026-09-08 by re-deriving from BASE.raw.
   8: #
   9: # The real baseline was provably clean regardless: the driver exits with
  10: #   "*** BASELINE NOT CLEAN -- table uninterpretable"
  11: # unless numerator == denominator, and it did not exit.  BASE.raw confirms 44/44 with its
  12: # completion sentinel present.
  13: #
  14: # Same class as the variable-shadowing bug that made this session's gate-edit script report
  15: # "+616 re-pinned" rows.  Both were caught by checking the OUTPUT against an independent
  16: # source rather than trusting the script that produced it.
  17: 
  18: mutant          score    floor  verdict   what it is
  19: M1_reinstate6   30/44    (b)    KILLED    restore fatal()+exit(1) at ALL SIX read arms, verbatim
  20: M2_datafill     42/44    (d)    KILLED    fill data[] instead of odata -- the tail overwrites it (the bug I nearly shipped)
  21: M3_noincr       42/44    (d)    KILLED    drop the tlbi++ -- four copies of one cell
  22: M4_readshift    43/44    (d)    KILLED    read-side index re-map >> 1 -> >> 2, write side untouched
  23: M5_shortloop    42/44    (d)    KILLED    shorten the read loop; the guard still tests len != 8
  24: M6_translate    41/44    (f)    KILLED    ANCHOR: +1 translation on BOTH store and read in TLB_A
  25: M7_farbound     43/44    (f)    KILLED    FAR-BOUND shrink of TLB_A -- invisible to a row at the window base
  26: M8_texaccept    40/44    (d)    KILLED    convert TEX to ACCEPT -- what the store-first TEX rows exist to catch
  27: M9_texnolatch   43/44    (d)    KILLED    remove the latch: announce per access instead of per instance
  28: M10_texbit      43/44    (d)    KILLED    CROSS-BIT: give the read decline the WIDTH latch instead of its own
  29: M11_lanerev     42/44    (d)    KILLED    reverse the halfword lane order -- VAL_HI differs in every lane
  30: M12_linswap     42/44    (d)    KILLED    swap the two LINEAR_A words -- the fixed-arity analogue of M11
  31: 
  32: NOT KILLED: none
  33: KILLTABLE_DONE
