 108: #  *** THE RE-PIN VALUES (sgirekills).  VAL_HI differs from VAL_LO in every
 109: #  halfword lane.
 110: #
 111: #  AN EARLIER WORDING CALLED THAT "the point of having two", claiming a single
 112: #  value, or two sharing any lane, "would let such an edit through".  THAT
 113: #  OVERCLAIMED, and the pass-2 panel caught it: VAL_LO ALONE already has four
 114: #  DISTINCT halfwords (1122 3344 5566 7788), so it by itself reddens under a
 115: #  pure read-side lane permutation or duplication -- M11_lanerev reds the lo
 116: #  row as well as the hi one, which is the measurement that settles it.
 117: #
 118: #  What the SECOND value actually buys is narrower and still worth having: two
 119: #  rows cannot both be satisfied by a mutant returning one fixed constant, and
 120: #  the hi row exercises the window's LAST SLOT -- which is what M4 and M7
 121: #  measured, and neither is a lane property at all. ***
