   1: **Q3 is (a): YES, the effects differ.** Section 1 is correct.
   2: 
   3: Alpha binds the callback to `alpha_invalidate_translation_caches` in [cpu_alpha.c](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_alpha.c:91). Its generated implementation comes from [tmp_alpha_tail.c](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/tmp_alpha_tail.c:26):
   4: 
   5: ```c
   6: #define DYNTRANS_INVALIDATE_TC alpha_invalidate_translation_caches
   7: #include "cpu_dyntrans.c"
   8: ```
   9: 
  10: The **64-bit VADDR branch** iterates over the cache using this condition, then returns. [cpu_dyntrans.c](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_dyntrans.c:1241):
  11: 
  12: ```c
  13: for (r=0; r<DYNTRANS_MAX_VPH_TLB_ENTRIES; r++)
  14: 	if (cpu->cd.DYNTRANS_ARCH.vph_tlb_entry[r].valid &&
  15: 	    (cpu->cd.DYNTRANS_ARCH.vph_tlb_entry[r].vaddr_page
  16: 	    & cpu->vaddr_mask) == (addr_page & cpu->vaddr_mask)) {
  17: 		DYNTRANS_INVALIDATE_TLB_ENTRY(cpu, cpu->cd.DYNTRANS_ARCH.vph_tlb_entry[r].vaddr_page, flags);
  18: 		n ++;
  19: 	}
  20: ```
  21: 
  22: The **ALL branch** has no address predicate. With comments omitted, [its implementation](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_dyntrans.c:1276) is:
  23: 
  24: ```c
  25: if (flags & INVALIDATE_ALL) {
  26: 	for (r=0; r<DYNTRANS_MAX_VPH_TLB_ENTRIES; r++) {
  27: 		if (cpu->cd.DYNTRANS_ARCH.vph_tlb_entry[r].valid) {
  28: 			DYNTRANS_INVALIDATE_TLB_ENTRY(cpu, cpu->cd.
  29: 			    DYNTRANS_ARCH.vph_tlb_entry[r].vaddr_page,
  30: 			    0);
  31: 		}
  32: 	}
  33: 	return;
  34: }
  35: ```
  36: 
  37: Those calls actually remove usable mappings. The [64-bit entry helper](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_dyntrans.c:1134) contains:
  38: 
  39: ```c
  40: l3->host_load[x3] = NULL;
  41: l3->host_store[x3] = NULL;
  42: l3->phys_addr[x3] = 0;
  43: l3->phys_page[x3] = NULL;
  44: if (l3->vaddr_to_tlbindex[x3] != 0) {
  45: 	cpu->cd.DYNTRANS_ARCH.vph_tlb_entry[
  46: 	    l3->vaddr_to_tlbindex[x3] - 1].valid = 0;
  47: ```
  48: 
  49: Consequently, the earlier comment claiming VADDR clears only the quick array is stale for this implementation.
  50: 
  51: Alpha uses **8 KiB pages**, and normal CPU construction gives it an **all-ones `vaddr_mask`**. Thus `ALPHA_TBIA()` currently invalidates only cached virtual page zero�?"nothing if that page is absent. Every other cached mapping survives. [Page size](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_alpha.c:50), [mask initialization](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu.c:140).
  52: 
  53: **The guest-visible consequence is stale translations surviving a flush the OS believes succeeded.** A previously cached, subsequently remapped nonzero virtual page can still access its old physical backing: Alpha�?Ts [load/store fast path](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_alpha_instr_loadstore.c:151) consumes those surviving host pointers.
  54: 
  55: An empty cache can make the two calls coincide; that does not make their semantics equivalent. �?oALL�?? here clears address-translation mappings, rather than discarding all separately cached compiled instructions.
  56: 
  57: **Q4: a witness is feasible from the source, but I have not established your required red/green witness.**
  58: 
  59: �?oNo Alpha paging rig exists�?? would be an incorrect disposition:
  60: 
  61: - [memory_alpha.c](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/memory_alpha.c:96) contains an active three-level page-table walker. The �?oNot yet implemented�?? diagnostic earlier in that file is inside a specific zero-PTBR bootstrap case.
  62: - [AlphaBook 1 is registered in-tree](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/machines/machine_alpha.c:242).
  63: - Existing [Alpha harness controls](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/alpha_harness_probe.py:180) cover guest memory liveness and PAL dispatch, and the [paging probe](/C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/alpha_pfnoffset_probe.py:125) uses the ordinary Alpha machine executable.
  64: 
  65: These establish an existing basis for testing, **not a completed `alphatbinegsel` differential**. I found no dedicated test in the searched regression sources and ran no before/after comparison. The defensible status is **source-confirmed functional defect; witness unvalidated**. Neither inherent unobservability nor absent paging support justifies closing it as documented-only.
  66: 
  67: **Q5: yes, I still recommend `if (a0 >= 1 && a0 <= 3)`.** It makes the defined negative selectors select full invalidation and preserves address-specific handling for selectors 1�?"3.
  68: 
  69: This is a **functional repair**. It retains coarse full flushing for `-1`; it does not implement selective preservation of global entries. After applying it, an accurate CHANGELOG claim would be:
  70: 
