1203:     #  those need different responses.
1204:     #  *** THE FIRST DRAFT OF THIS BLOCK HAD TWO DEFECTS, BOTH FOUND BY THE PASS-2 SEAT.
1205:     #  (1) It ended in `|| true`, which is INERT: check() in lib.sh has no `return`, so
1206:     #  it exits 0 on BOTH branches and the row counts into _fails regardless.  The
1207:     #  suppression never existed -- but a reader would conclude that row was advisory,
1208:     #  which is worse than either behaviour on its own.
1209:     #  (2) The denominator concatenated two counts and compared to "350" -- satisfied by
1210:     #  (35 ok, 0 FAIL) AND by (3 ok, 50 FAIL).  A string join is not an arithmetic
1211:     #  identity, and it was redundant with the two rows below it anyway. ***
1212:     #  *** AND THE FIRST REPAIR OF (2) REPRODUCED THE VERY DEFECT THE PANEL HAD JUST FOUND
1213:     #  IN THIS ROUND'S BRIEF.  I wrote `count "$SGILOG" " ok$| FAIL$"` -- but count() is
1214:     #  `grep -ac`, PLAIN grep, so `|` is a LITERAL and the pattern matches NOTHING.
1215:     #  Measured: 0 against a log holding 35 rows.  The seats had flagged `grep -i
1216:     #  'sgi|width'` in the brief for exactly this, one hour earlier. ***
1217:     #
1218:     #  Summed ARITHMETICALLY instead, which needs no regex dialect at all -- and unlike the
1219:     #  string-concatenation form it replaces, it cannot be satisfied by (3 ok, 50 FAIL).
1220:     check "sgi_re rows emitted" \
1221:           "$(( $(count "$SGILOG" " ok$") + $(count "$SGILOG" " FAIL$") ))" "46"
1222:     check "sgi_re rows green"   "$(count "$SGILOG" " ok$")"   "46"
1223:     check "sgi_re rows red"     "$(count "$SGILOG" " FAIL$")" "0"
 486: #  *** THE ROW PROVES ITS OWN SETUP.  This is the repair for the defect that made it vacuous. ***
 487: #  Counting only the TEX decline cannot distinguish "ten latches fired and TEX still announced"
 488: #  from "the setup did nothing and TEX announced".  Both give 1.  So the row also reports HOW MANY
 489: #  of the other announces it actually saw, and wants ALL of them: a setup that silently fails --
 490: #  a mistyped call, a moved register, a changed message -- now REDS this row instead of passing it.
