_scratchpad/panel_sgirekills_pass3_20260908/ollama_glm.txt:13:- (REASONED) A retarget to an *unused* bit is behaviour-preserving (equivalent) — that is why the breach needed an already-used bit. A retarget to in-use bit k is observable only where class(k)'s event and a TEX read decline co-fire in one instance, and killable only by a row that co-fires them.
