_scratchpad/panel_sgirekills_pass3_20260908/ollama_glm.txt:22:- (REASONED) The #392 rebuttal: a rule demanding a row per bit *pair among all twelve classes* would be #392. Demanding kills for every operand mutant of an **edited** line is just the floor's definition. And no pairwise explosion is needed: the detector's own idiom — one `tex xbit` session pre-setting six bits, killing six destinations in one row — generalizes. One session firing the classes at 6, 7, 9, 10 before a TEX read kills all four retargets at once. If a class's event cannot be fired alongside a TEX read, record the equivalence. Decision procedure, not row-per-pair.
