_scratchpad/panel_sgirekills_pass3_20260908/grok.txt:1:I'll review the pass-2 repair against the shipped composite, starting with the detector, the two new rows, and the comment corrections rather than ratifying from the log.I have the probe and the device file; next I’ll read the repair, the latch enum, and the pass-2 brief so the review is against the shipped composite.The detector and enum are in view; next I’ll walk the access function and the pass-2 panel so the floor sweep is against real guards, not the brief’s summary.Pass 2 closed bit 8 in both orders; I’ll check whether bits 6, 7, 9 and 10 are the same cell, and whether the new rows can go green while the latch is still wrong.The repair closed bit 8 and left the write twin; I’ll check how cheaply the other live `d->warned` bits can be raised so one row can close the class.The pass-2 rows only pair bit 11 with bit 8; aliasing `SGIRE_W_TEX_RD` onto bit 7 (or 6, 9, 10) still sweeps 46/46. I’ll close that class with one field-wide row, not a row per pair, and fix the contract text the last correction left looking live.**DO NOT SHIP.** The pass-2 repair reproduced the breach it closed: it rowed both *orders* of one colliding bit and left the rest of `d->warned` unswept. `SGIRE_W_TEX_RD = 1 << 7` (`SGIRE_W_UNMAP_WR`) still sweeps the 46-row detector clean. Same class as M13, same function, and this detector already stores to `OUTSIDE` — just never in the same instance as a TEX read.
