 177: 	 *  PLACED LAST, DELIBERATELY, AND THE ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING.
 178: 	 *  re_linear_a/b are written at [tlbi] AND [tlbi+1] with tlbi able to
 179: 	 *  reach 31, so index 32 of either array lands on whichever field
 180: 	 *  FOLLOWS it.  An earlier draft of this change put `warned' between
 181: 	 *  re_linear_b and de_reg; measured with offsetof, that made
 182: 	 *  re_linear_b[32] alias `warned' rather than de_reg[0] -- which both
 183: 	 *  falsified the adjacency the two LINEAR site comments cite, and made
 184: 	 *  an over-run SET WARNING LATCH BITS and silence this device's own
 185: 	 *  diagnostics.  Keeping the latch after mte_reg restores the
 186: 	 *  documented adjacency: re_linear_a[32] is re_linear_b[0] and
 187: 	 *  re_linear_b[32] is de_reg[0].
 207: void horrible_getputpixel(int put, struct cpu* cpu, struct sgi_re_data* d,
