  89: 
  90: ## Q5. DECLINE is right; the warrant's "breaking oracle / round left free" half is overstated
  91: 
  92: **Against, as asked.**
  93: 
  94: Member 4 of the option set does apply: the write arm already stores a value. Calling the read "unimplemented" is a stretch - the register is modelled; the **index** is untrusted. A mirrored ACCEPT (`>> 3` on both sides) round-trips a single `sd`/`ld` at one address, which is what a save/restore of that register would do. Overlap corruption is `sgitexindex`'s defect, already filed.
  95: 
  96: The "future `sgitexindex` becomes a breaking oracle change" argument is **already true of a row this detector shipped before this round.** `SITES` for TEX is:
  97: 
  98: ```python
  99: ("tex", 0xb5001600, "CRIME_RE_TEX", "d->re_tex[1] = 0x1122"),
 100: ```
 101: 
 102: Probed at **+8**. TLB siblings at +8 want `[4]` (`8 >> 1`). TEX wants `[1]` (`8 >> 3`). That **is** the missing factor of four, already pinned on the write. When `sgitexindex` moves both arms to `>> 1`, `tex accept` reds regardless of whether this round ACCEPTed the read.
 103: 
 104: Worse: a **value-only** mirrored ACCEPT at the same address would *survive* a both-sides `>> 3`  `>> 1` change (the cells move; the address still round-trips). Decline is not what keeps that round free. `tex accept` already doesn't.
 105: 
 106: **Still decline, on the parts of the warrant that survive that.**
 107: 
 108: - Do-not-code means **do not copy `>> 3` onto a second site.** Mirrored ACCEPT doubles the typo.
 109: - `re_tex` has no consumer. A guest-visible read of the aliased map is a new lie; zeros plus `unimplemented read from CRIME_RE_TEX -- declined` is an old, named one.
 110: - Plausible-looking garbage at overlapping offsets is worse than zeros. M8 (`40/44`) shows the store-first rows do the job they were written for: ACCEPT returns `VAL_*` and they red. A load-only `v0==0` oracle would not have.
 111: 
 112: So: decline, but not because it leaves `sgitexindex` a clean slate. It doesn't. Re-pin `tex accept` when that round happens; these four TEX rows stay until someone has a consumer.
