regress/artifacts/armbfiwidth/codex_fixdesign_20260908.txt:1:**Verdict: extend `#510` with a nonpositive-width guard. The original 468 UB pairs are correct; copying `#510` verbatim leaves 465 undefined, not 467.**
regress/artifacts/armbfiwidth/codex_fixdesign_20260908.txt:39:- Original UB: `465 + 2 + 1 = 468`.
regress/artifacts/armbfiwidth/codex_fixdesign_20260908.txt:40:- Reversed ordering: `465 + 31 = 496`.
regress/artifacts/armbfiwidth/codex_fixdesign_20260908.txt:41:- Their intersection: **465**.
regress/artifacts/armbfiwidth/codex_fixdesign_20260908.txt:61:| `< 0` | 465 | Undefined | Zero mask; destination unchanged |
regress/artifacts/armbfiwidth/codex_fixdesign_20260908.txt:69:**No currently defined pair changes behavior.** For all 556 such pairs, the mask is numerically identical, so the unchanged destination-update statements produce identical results for every source and destination value. Enumeration also found zero mismatches against an independently constructed, bit-by-bit field mask across all 1024 pairs.
regress/artifacts/armbfiwidth/codex_fixdesign_20260908.txt:75:Your [CPU build Makefile](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/build-asan/src/cpus/Makefile:9) already specifies `-fsanitize=address,undefined`; this configuration includes UBSan. ASan alone would not detect this arithmetic UB. Also, **468 counts input pairs, not expected diagnostic lines**.
regress/artifacts/armbfiwidth/FIXDESIGN_brief.md:27:Over all **1024** encodable `(msb, lsb)` pairs:
regress/artifacts/armbfiwidth/FIXDESIGN_brief.md:29:    width < 0     465   UNDEFINED  (negative shift count)
regress/artifacts/armbfiwidth/FIXDESIGN_brief.md:30:    width == 0     31   DEFINED    -- 1 << 0 is 1; mask becomes 0
regress/artifacts/armbfiwidth/FIXDESIGN_brief.md:35:    UNDEFINED     468
regress/artifacts/armbfiwidth/FIXDESIGN_brief.md:37:The 496 pairs with `msb < lsb` (architecturally invalid field ordering) OVERLAP this set by 465 --
regress/artifacts/armbfiwidth/FIXDESIGN_brief.md:38:they are not disjoint populations. **You corrected an earlier version of this row that said 499;
regress/artifacts/armbfiwidth/FIXDESIGN_brief.md:39:check the 468 too.**
regress/artifacts/armbfiwidth/FIXDESIGN_brief.md:53:would leave 467 of the 468 undefined pairs undefined. Derive each handler's width domain from its
regress/artifacts/armbfiwidth/FIXDESIGN_brief.md:63:**Q4. Give the smallest repair that makes every one of the 1024 pairs defined**, in the style of the

