5: ## Premises (section 1)
6: 
7: All six claims hold. Two footnotes, neither of which undoes the defect:
8: 
9: 1. **`a0` is an unsigned compare of `-2`.** `alpha_palcode()` copies `cpu->cd.alpha.r[ALPHA_A0]` into a `uint64_t a0` and then does `if (a0 >= 1)` with no signed cast (`cpu_alpha_palcode.c`). `ALPHA_TBIA()` is `alpha_pal_tbi(-2, 0)` (`src/include/thirdparty/alpha_cpu.h`). `-2` is `0xfffffffffffffffe`, which is `>= 1`, so the call takes `INVALIDATE_VADDR` with `a1 = 0`.
10: 
11: 2. **The two invalidate arms really differ.** VADDR keeps an entry only when `(vaddr_page & vaddr_mask) == (addr_page & vaddr_mask)`; ALL walks every valid entry with no address test (`cpu_dyntrans.c`). Alpha is 8 KiB (`DYNTRANS_8K` in `cpu_alpha.c`) and `vaddr_mask` is the `cpu.c` default `(int64_t)-1` because `cpu_alpha.c` never sets it (`is_32bit = 0`). So `ALPHA_TBIA()` invalidates **cached virtual page 0 only**.
12: 
13:    The comment that VADDR "only clears the quick array, not `vph_tlb_entry[]`" is stale. The 64-bit helper **does** NULL `host_load` / `host_store` / `phys_addr` / `phys_page` and clear `valid`. The bug is **which** entries are selected, not that the helper is a no-op.
14: 
15: 3. **The fast path consumes those pointers.** `LS_N` indexes `l3->host_load[x3]` (store: `host_store`); NULL falls through to `LS_GENERIC_N`  `memory_rw` (`cpu_alpha_instr_loadstore.c`).
16: 
17: `ALPHA_TBIAP()` (`-1, 0`) is the same wrap. The ALL arm also does not implement ASM=0. That is extra, not a contradiction.
18: 
